-- title:
--   Sub-unit slope bound for the logarithm under nilpotent Hasse–Witt
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a commutative ring, $p$ a prime whose image in $\mathcal O$ is a non-zero-divisor, and suppose $\mathcal O$ carries an algebra structure over $\mathbb Z/p$ whose structure map has kernel exactly the ideal $(p)$. Let $F$ be a $d$-dimensional formal group law over $\mathcal O$, that is, a $d$-tuple `F.toPowerSeries` of power series in the variables indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\,d \oplus \mathrm{Fin}\,d$ with vanishing constant terms, with $\mathrm{coeff}$ of each degree-one monomial in the left (resp. right) block equal to $\delta_{ij}$, and satisfying the associativity identity; assume $F$ is commutative in the sense that swapping the two blocks of variables fixes each component. Let $Fp$ be a $d$-tuple of power series in the same $2d$ variables with zero constant coefficients such that for every nonzero multidegree $m$ one has $\mathrm{coeff}_m(Fp_i)\cdot p = p^{|m|}\,\mathrm{coeff}_m(F_i)$, where $|m|$ is the total degree (so $Fp$ is the rescaling $p^{-1}F(pX,pY)$). Let $\varphi$ be a $d$-tuple of power series in $d$ variables with zero constant coefficients whose linear part [`MvFormalGroup.linearPart`](def/MvFormalGroup_BasicV2.html#L359) is the identity matrix and which is additive for $Fp$: substituting $Fp$ into $\varphi_i$ equals $\varphi_i(X_{\mathrm{inl}}) + \varphi_i(X_{\mathrm{inr}})$. Finally assume that the $d \times d$ matrix over $\mathbb Z/p$ whose $(i,j)$ entry is the image of the coefficient of $X_j^{p}$ in the $p$-th iterate `F.nthSeries p i` (defined by $[0]=0$, $[n+1]_i = F_i([n], X)$) is nilpotent. Then there exist natural numbers $A, B, C$ with $A < B$ such that for all $i$ and all nonzero $m$, the coefficient $\mathrm{coeff}_m(\varphi_i)$ lies in the ideal generated by $p^{(|m|-1) - \lfloor A\lfloor\log_p|m|\rfloor/B\rfloor - C}$, the exponent being computed with truncated subtraction and division of natural numbers.
--
--   This is the analytic expression of unipotence for the formal group $F$: the coefficients of its logarithm $\varphi$ have $p$-adic valuations bounded below by $-(A/B)\log_p|m| - C$ with slope $A/B < 1$, in contrast with $\widehat{\mathbb G}_m$, whose logarithm has coefficients $\pm 1/m$ of slope $1$. It combines the divisibility of the logarithm coefficients coming from the additivity of $\varphi$ with the degree-raising estimate supplied by nilpotency of the Hasse–Witt matrix, and is used for the convergence of the rescaled exponential and in the covector description of the logarithm.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_MvFormalGroup_exists_coeff_mem_span_pow_sub_log_of_isNilpotent_hasseWitt.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_MvFormalGroup_BasicV2

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false
open MvPowerSeries

universe u

theorem MvFormalGroup.exists_coeff_mem_span_pow_sub_log_of_isNilpotent_hasseWitt
    {𝓞 : Type u} [CommRing 𝓞] (p : ℕ) [Fact p.Prime] (hp : (p : 𝓞) ∈ nonZeroDivisors 𝓞)
    [Algebra 𝓞 (ZMod p)] (hker : RingHom.ker (algebraMap 𝓞 (ZMod p)) = Ideal.span {(p : 𝓞)})
    {d : ℕ} (F : MvFormalGroup d 𝓞) [F.IsComm]
    (Fp : Fin d → MvPowerSeries (Fin d ⊕ Fin d) 𝓞)
    (hFp : ∀ (i : Fin d) (m : (Fin d ⊕ Fin d) →₀ ℕ), m ≠ 0 →
      (Fp i).coeff m * (p : 𝓞) = (p : 𝓞) ^ m.degree * (F.toPowerSeries i).coeff m)
    (hFp0 : ∀ i, (Fp i).constantCoeff = 0)
    (φ : Fin d → MvPowerSeries (Fin d) 𝓞)
    (hφ0 : ∀ i, (φ i).constantCoeff = 0)
    (hφ1 : MvFormalGroup.linearPart φ = 1)
    (hφF : ∀ i, subst Fp (φ i) =
      subst (fun j => (X (Sum.inl j) : MvPowerSeries (Fin d ⊕ Fin d) 𝓞)) (φ i) +
        subst (fun j => (X (Sum.inr j) : MvPowerSeries (Fin d ⊕ Fin d) 𝓞)) (φ i))
    (hHW : IsNilpotent (Matrix.of fun i j : Fin d =>
      algebraMap 𝓞 (ZMod p) ((F.nthSeries p i).coeff (Finsupp.single j p)))) :
    ∃ A B C : ℕ, A < B ∧ ∀ (i : Fin d) (m : Fin d →₀ ℕ), m ≠ 0 →
      (φ i).coeff m ∈ Ideal.span {(p : 𝓞) ^ ((m.degree - 1) - (A * Nat.log p m.degree) / B - C)} := by sorry
